  "note": "Checked: η₂' is 4/x on (1/4,1/2) and −4/x on (1/2,1), so it jumps by +16, −16, +4 at 1/4, 1/2, 1, and the smooth part is ∓4x⁻². Numerically, (2πt)²η̂₂(t) = eta2DD(t) = −(4g+f̂)(t) to 10⁻¹⁰ at t = 0.7, 3.1, 17.41. |η₂''|₁ = 36 + 12 = 48, as the book says."
